From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PatchForge
Date: Sat, 6 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accept Tag namedtuples in RepoGraph.tag_to_graph

get_ranked_tags yields Tag namedtuples, but tag_to_graph indexes
them as dicts (tag['name']), raising
TypeError: tuple indices must be integers or slices, not str
for every repository on every OS. (__main__ itself uses attribute
access, confirming namedtuples are the intended element type.)

Fix: normalize each tag via _asdict() when available, so both
namedtuples and plain dicts work. Single-point change; graph
semantics untouched.

Apply from the RepoGraph clone root:
  git apply <workspace>/patches/repograph-tag-dict-access.patch

Revert:
  git -C third_party/RepoGraph checkout -- repograph/construct_graph.py
  (then re-apply the other repograph-*.patch files if still needed)

Upstream status: not fixed upstream as of 2026-09-06.
Do NOT commit into third_party/; this file is the record (§24).

--- a/repograph/construct_graph.py
+++ b/repograph/construct_graph.py
@@ -95,5 +95,8 @@
     def tag_to_graph(self, tags):
-        
+
         G = nx.MultiDiGraph()
+        # get_ranked_tags yields Tag namedtuples; normalize so both
+        # namedtuples and dicts can be consumed below.
+        tags = [tag._asdict() if hasattr(tag, "_asdict") else tag for tag in tags]
         for tag in tags:
             G.add_node(tag['name'], category=tag['category'], info=tag['info'], fname=tag['fname'], line=tag['line'], kind=tag['kind'])
